      },
      "message": "[Clean-up] Clean-ing pseudo code description of register value when the register index is x0\n\nWhen x0 is used to index a pair of registers, the specification specifies that both the low and the high XLEN-bit\nshould be interpreted as zero-values.\n\nThis patch is an attempts at cleaning this in the P extension specification.\nIt introduces a very verbose prolog for a lot of instructions.",
